  "final": "Done. The cause was float math in `billing/totals.py` `line_total_cents`.\n\nPrices like 0.15 with 10% tax come out as 16.4999… cents in binary floating point, so `round` dropped them to 16 instead of the half-up 17 the README promises. A scan of 1,200 price and tax combinations found 86 that were off by a cent.\n\nI switched the calculation to `Decimal` with `ROUND_HALF_UP`. The invoice total uses the same function, so it's fixed too. I added a regression test, `test_half_cent_rounds_up`.\n\nAll 7 tests pass with the fix. With the fix stashed, the new test fails.\n\nI didn't run the CLI against a real CSV.",
